    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0450" n="334" xml:id="pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">719.21/57</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Colombian, Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Olaya</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Chief of the Division of Latin American Affairs, Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >White</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1063</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. White</hi>: Referring to your esteemed
                    letter of the 12th inst., and to our last conversation in your office, I take
                    pleasure in advising you that my Government approves the text of the Procès
                    Verbal for initiating regular diplomatic relations between Colombia and Panama
                    as submitted by the Department of State, and authorizes me to sign it.</p>
                <p>It gives me great pleasure to have reached this happy result and trusting to hear
                    from you in the matter, I await your commands and remain,</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Enrique Olaya</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
